    <item ident="g83de683dbc81701663baff8411876769" title="Question 1">
      <itemmetadata>
        <qtimetadata>
          <qtimetadatafield>
            <fieldlabel>question_type</fieldlabel>
            <fieldentry>multiple_choice_question</fieldentry>
          </qtimetadatafield>
          <qtimetadatafield>
            <fieldlabel>points_possible</fieldlabel>
            <fieldentry>1</fieldentry>
          </qtimetadatafield>
          <qtimetadatafield>
            <fieldlabel>original_answer_ids</fieldlabel>
            <fieldentry>10635,51051,88525,55169</fieldentry>
          </qtimetadatafield>
        </qtimetadata>
      </itemmetadata>
      <presentation>
        <material>
          <mattext texttype="text/html">&lt;div&gt;What is reflective writing?&lt;/div&gt;</mattext>
        </material>
        <response_lid ident="response1" rcardinality="Single">
          <render_choice>
            <response_label ident="10635">
              <material>
                <mattext texttype="text/plain">The practice of thinking about an experience and expressing its larger meaning from your own perspective.</mattext>
              </material>
            </response_label>
            <response_label ident="51051">
              <material>
                <mattext texttype="text/plain">The practice of summarizing and synthesizing information from outside sources.</mattext>
              </material>
            </response_label>
            <response_label ident="88525">
              <material>
                <mattext texttype="text/plain">The practice of writing a formal argument supported by evidence, such as facts and statistics.</mattext>
              </material>
            </response_label>
            <response_label ident="55169">
              <material>
                <mattext texttype="text/plain">The practice of describing an event in detail without analyzing its meaning or significance.</mattext>
              </material>
            </response_label>
          </render_choice>
        </response_lid>
      </presentation>
      <resprocessing>
        <outcomes>
          <decvar maxvalue="100" minvalue="0" varname="SCORE" vartype="Decimal"/>
        </outcomes>
        <respcondition continue="Yes">
          <conditionvar>
            <varequal respident="response1">51051</varequal>
          </conditionvar>
          <displayfeedback feedbacktype="Response" linkrefid="51051_fb"/>
        </respcondition>
        <respcondition continue="Yes">
          <conditionvar>
            <varequal respident="response1">88525</varequal>
          </conditionvar>
          <displayfeedback feedbacktype="Response" linkrefid="88525_fb"/>
        </respcondition>
        <respcondition continue="Yes">
          <conditionvar>
            <varequal respident="response1">55169</varequal>
          </conditionvar>
          <displayfeedback feedbacktype="Response" linkrefid="55169_fb"/>
        </respcondition>
        <respcondition continue="No">
          <conditionvar>
            <varequal respident="response1">10635</varequal>
          </conditionvar>
          <setvar action="Set" varname="SCORE">100</setvar>
        </respcondition>
      </resprocessing>
      <itemfeedback ident="51051_fb">
        <flow_mat>
          <material>
            <mattext texttype="text/plain">Reflective writing goes beyond summary or argument. It asks the writer to examine a personal experience and explain what it means and how it changed them. Summarizing outside sources describes research writing, not reflective writing. Arguing with facts and statistics describes argumentative writing. Describing an event without analysis is a summary, which is one of the most common misconceptions about reflective writing.</mattext>
          </material>
        </flow_mat>
      </itemfeedback>
      <itemfeedback ident="88525_fb">
        <flow_mat>
          <material>
            <mattext texttype="text/plain">Reflective writing goes beyond summary or argument. It asks the writer to examine a personal experience and explain what it means and how it changed them. Summarizing outside sources describes research writing, not reflective writing. Arguing with facts and statistics describes argumentative writing. Describing an event without analysis is a summary, which is one of the most common misconceptions about reflective writing.</mattext>
          </material>
        </flow_mat>
      </itemfeedback>
      <itemfeedback ident="55169_fb">
        <flow_mat>
          <material>
            <mattext texttype="text/plain">Reflective writing goes beyond summary or argument. It asks the writer to examine a personal experience and explain what it means and how it changed them. Summarizing outside sources describes research writing, not reflective writing. Arguing with facts and statistics describes argumentative writing. Describing an event without analysis is a summary, which is one of the most common misconceptions about reflective writing.</mattext>
          </material>
        </flow_mat>
      </itemfeedback>
    </item>
    <item ident="gf65ed6601bb7950dbb0b2a38b4989e08" title="Question 10">
      <itemmetadata>
        <qtimetadata>
          <qtimetadatafield>
            <fieldlabel>question_type</fieldlabel>
            <fieldentry>multiple_choice_question</fieldentry>
          </qtimetadatafield>
          <qtimetadatafield>
            <fieldlabel>points_possible</fieldlabel>
            <fieldentry>1</fieldentry>
          </qtimetadatafield>
          <qtimetadatafield>
            <fieldlabel>original_answer_ids</fieldlabel>
            <fieldentry>17935,37921,81528,59918</fieldentry>
          </qtimetadatafield>
        </qtimetadata>
      </itemmetadata>
      <presentation>
        <material>
          <mattext texttype="text/html">&lt;div&gt;What question does reflective writing answer that a personal narrative does not?&lt;/div&gt;</mattext>
        </material>
        <response_lid ident="response1" rcardinality="Single">
          <render_choice>
            <response_label ident="17935">
              <material>
                <mattext texttype="text/plain">What happened, why does it matter, and what will I do about it?</mattext>
              </material>
            </response_label>
            <response_label ident="37921">
              <material>
                <mattext texttype="text/plain">What happened and who was involved?</mattext>
              </material>
            </response_label>
            <response_label ident="81528">
              <material>
                <mattext texttype="text/plain">What is the writer's main argument?</mattext>
              </material>
            </response_label>
            <response_label ident="59918">
              <material>
                <mattext texttype="text/plain">What sources support the writer's experience?</mattext>
              </material>
            </response_label>
          </render_choice>
        </response_lid>
      </presentation>
      <resprocessing>
        <outcomes>
          <decvar maxvalue="100" minvalue="0" varname="SCORE" vartype="Decimal"/>
        </outcomes>
        <respcondition continue="Yes">
          <conditionvar>
            <varequal respident="response1">37921</varequal>
          </conditionvar>
          <displayfeedback feedbacktype="Response" linkrefid="37921_fb"/>
        </respcondition>
        <respcondition continue="Yes">
          <conditionvar>
            <varequal respident="response1">81528</varequal>
          </conditionvar>
          <displayfeedback feedbacktype="Response" linkrefid="81528_fb"/>
        </respcondition>
        <respcondition continue="Yes">
          <conditionvar>
            <varequal respident="response1">59918</varequal>
          </conditionvar>
          <displayfeedback feedbacktype="Response" linkrefid="59918_fb"/>
        </respcondition>
        <respcondition continue="No">
          <conditionvar>
            <varequal respident="response1">17935</varequal>
          </conditionvar>
          <setvar action="Set" varname="SCORE">100</setvar>
        </respcondition>
      </resprocessing>
      <itemfeedback ident="37921_fb">
        <flow_mat>
          <material>
            <mattext texttype="text/plain">A personal narrative answers the question "What happened?" Reflective writing goes further by also answering why the experience matters and what the writer will do as a result. Identifying who was involved is part of storytelling, not reflection. A main argument is the focus of argumentative writing. Sources are used in research writing, not reflective writing.</mattext>
          </material>
        </flow_mat>
      </itemfeedback>
      <itemfeedback ident="81528_fb">
        <flow_mat>
          <material>
            <mattext texttype="text/plain">A personal narrative answers the question "What happened?" Reflective writing goes further by also answering why the experience matters and what the writer will do as a result. Identifying who was involved is part of storytelling, not reflection. A main argument is the focus of argumentative writing. Sources are used in research writing, not reflective writing.</mattext>
          </material>
        </flow_mat>
      </itemfeedback>
      <itemfeedback ident="59918_fb">
        <flow_mat>
          <material>
            <mattext texttype="text/plain">A personal narrative answers the question "What happened?" Reflective writing goes further by also answering why the experience matters and what the writer will do as a result. Identifying who was involved is part of storytelling, not reflection. A main argument is the focus of argumentative writing. Sources are used in research writing, not reflective writing.</mattext>
          </material>
        </flow_mat>
      </itemfeedback>
    </item>
    <item ident="g29716cd0a251ffa85bec161fdea99fe0" title="Question 11">
      <itemmetadata>
        <qtimetadata>
          <qtimetadatafield>
            <fieldlabel>question_type</fieldlabel>
            <fieldentry>multiple_choice_question</fieldentry>
          </qtimetadatafield>
          <qtimetadatafield>
            <fieldlabel>points_possible</fieldlabel>
            <fieldentry>1</fieldentry>
          </qtimetadatafield>
          <qtimetadatafield>
            <fieldlabel>original_answer_ids</fieldlabel>
            <fieldentry>87467,96906,29771,33811</fieldentry>
          </qtimetadatafield>
        </qtimetadata>
      </itemmetadata>
      <presentation>
        <material>
          <mattext texttype="text/html">&lt;div&gt;What does the term "introspection" mean?&lt;/div&gt;</mattext>
        </material>
        <response_lid ident="response1" rcardinality="Single">
          <render_choice>
            <response_label ident="87467">
              <material>
                <mattext texttype="text/plain">The examination of one's own thoughts and feelings.</mattext>
              </material>
            </response_label>
            <response_label ident="96906">
              <material>
                <mattext texttype="text/plain">The process of gathering information from outside sources.</mattext>
              </material>
            </response_label>
            <response_label ident="29771">
              <material>
                <mattext texttype="text/plain">The act of writing a summary of an experience.</mattext>
              </material>
            </response_label>
            <response_label ident="33811">
              <material>
                <mattext texttype="text/plain">The process of editing a draft for grammar errors.</mattext>
              </material>
            </response_label>
          </render_choice>
        </response_lid>
      </presentation>
      <resprocessing>
        <outcomes>
          <decvar maxvalue="100" minvalue="0" varname="SCORE" vartype="Decimal"/>
        </outcomes>
        <respcondition continue="Yes">
          <conditionvar>
            <varequal respident="response1">96906</varequal>
          </conditionvar>
          <displayfeedback feedbacktype="Response" linkrefid="96906_fb"/>
        </respcondition>
        <respcondition continue="Yes">
          <conditionvar>
            <varequal respident="response1">29771</varequal>
          </conditionvar>
          <displayfeedback feedbacktype="Response" linkrefid="29771_fb"/>
        </respcondition>
        <respcondition continue="Yes">
          <conditionvar>
            <varequal respident="response1">33811</varequal>
          </conditionvar>
          <displayfeedback feedbacktype="Response" linkrefid="33811_fb"/>
        </respcondition>
        <respcondition continue="No">
          <conditionvar>
            <varequal respident="response1">87467</varequal>
          </conditionvar>
          <setvar action="Set" varname="SCORE">100</setvar>
        </respcondition>
      </resprocessing>
      <itemfeedback ident="96906_fb">
        <flow_mat>
          <material>
            <mattext texttype="text/plain">Introspection is defined in the chapter vocabulary as the examination of one's own thoughts and feelings. Gathering outside information describes research. Summarizing an experience is part of the exploration stage but is not what introspection means. Editing for grammar errors is part of the revision process.</mattext>
          </material>
        </flow_mat>
      </itemfeedback>
      <itemfeedback ident="29771_fb">
        <flow_mat>
          <material>
            <mattext texttype="text/plain">Introspection is defined in the chapter vocabulary as the examination of one's own thoughts and feelings. Gathering outside information describes research. Summarizing an experience is part of the exploration stage but is not what introspection means. Editing for grammar errors is part of the revision process.</mattext>
          </material>
        </flow_mat>
      </itemfeedback>
      <itemfeedback ident="33811_fb">
        <flow_mat>
          <material>
            <mattext texttype="text/plain">Introspection is defined in the chapter vocabulary as the examination of one's own thoughts and feelings. Gathering outside information describes research. Summarizing an experience is part of the exploration stage but is not what introspection means. Editing for grammar errors is part of the revision process.</mattext>
          </material>
        </flow_mat>
      </itemfeedback>
    </item>
    <item ident="g61b31e73fbba2d7bdd53b156b995119f" title="Question 12">
      <itemmetadata>
        <qtimetadata>
          <qtimetadatafield>
            <fieldlabel>question_type</fieldlabel>
            <fieldentry>multiple_choice_question</fieldentry>
          </qtimetadatafield>
          <qtimetadatafield>
            <fieldlabel>points_possible</fieldlabel>
            <fieldentry>1</fieldentry>
          </qtimetadatafield>
          <qtimetadatafield>
            <fieldlabel>original_answer_ids</fieldlabel>
            <fieldentry>94520,48624,48893,40023</fieldentry>
          </qtimetadatafield>
        </qtimetadata>
      </itemmetadata>
      <presentation>
        <material>
          <mattext texttype="text/html">&lt;div&gt;What is an epiphany in the context of reflective writing?&lt;/div&gt;</mattext>
        </material>
        <response_lid ident="response1" rcardinality="Single">
          <render_choice>
            <response_label ident="94520">
              <material>
                <mattext texttype="text/plain">A sudden realization or insight.</mattext>
              </material>
            </response_label>
            <response_label ident="48624">
              <material>
                <mattext texttype="text/plain">A formal thesis statement placed at the beginning of an essay.</mattext>
              </material>
            </response_label>
            <response_label ident="48893">
              <material>
                <mattext texttype="text/plain">A transition sentence that connects two paragraphs.</mattext>
              </material>
            </response_label>
            <response_label ident="40023">
              <material>
                <mattext texttype="text/plain">A summary of the main points at the end of an essay.</mattext>
              </material>
            </response_label>
          </render_choice>
        </response_lid>
      </presentation>
      <resprocessing>
        <outcomes>
          <decvar maxvalue="100" minvalue="0" varname="SCORE" vartype="Decimal"/>
        </outcomes>
        <respcondition continue="Yes">
          <conditionvar>
            <varequal respident="response1">48624</varequal>
          </conditionvar>
          <displayfeedback feedbacktype="Response" linkrefid="48624_fb"/>
        </respcondition>
        <respcondition continue="Yes">
          <conditionvar>
            <varequal respident="response1">48893</varequal>
          </conditionvar>
          <displayfeedback feedbacktype="Response" linkrefid="48893_fb"/>
        </respcondition>
        <respcondition continue="Yes">
          <conditionvar>
            <varequal respident="response1">40023</varequal>
          </conditionvar>
          <displayfeedback feedbacktype="Response" linkrefid="40023_fb"/>
        </respcondition>
        <respcondition continue="No">
          <conditionvar>
            <varequal respident="response1">94520</varequal>
          </conditionvar>
          <setvar action="Set" varname="SCORE">100</setvar>
        </respcondition>
      </resprocessing>
      <itemfeedback ident="48624_fb">
        <flow_mat>
          <material>
            <mattext texttype="text/plain">The chapter defines an epiphany as a sudden realization or insight. In reflective writing, this often appears near the end of the essay as the writer works through the meaning of an experience. A thesis statement, transition sentence, and concluding summary are structural elements of other types of writing, not the definition of epiphany.</mattext>
          </material>
        </flow_mat>
      </itemfeedback>
      <itemfeedback ident="48893_fb">
        <flow_mat>
          <material>
            <mattext texttype="text/plain">The chapter defines an epiphany as a sudden realization or insight. In reflective writing, this often appears near the end of the essay as the writer works through the meaning of an experience. A thesis statement, transition sentence, and concluding summary are structural elements of other types of writing, not the definition of epiphany.</mattext>
          </material>
        </flow_mat>
      </itemfeedback>
      <itemfeedback ident="40023_fb">
        <flow_mat>
          <material>
            <mattext texttype="text/plain">The chapter defines an epiphany as a sudden realization or insight. In reflective writing, this often appears near the end of the essay as the writer works through the meaning of an experience. A thesis statement, transition sentence, and concluding summary are structural elements of other types of writing, not the definition of epiphany.</mattext>
          </material>
        </flow_mat>
      </itemfeedback>
    </item>
    <item ident="gbd9f8cd95617e9a7caa9b7082f69899d" title="Question 13">
      <itemmetadata>
        <qtimetadata>
          <qtimetadatafield>
            <fieldlabel>question_type</fieldlabel>
            <fieldentry>multiple_choice_question</fieldentry>
          </qtimetadatafield>
          <qtimetadatafield>
            <fieldlabel>points_possible</fieldlabel>
            <fieldentry>1</fieldentry>
          </qtimetadatafield>
          <qtimetadatafield>
            <fieldlabel>original_answer_ids</fieldlabel>
            <fieldentry>3637,28594,52973,92315</fieldentry>
          </qtimetadatafield>
        </qtimetadata>
      </itemmetadata>
      <presentation>
        <material>
          <mattext texttype="text/html">&lt;div&gt;What writing voice does reflective writing primarily use?&lt;/div&gt;</mattext>
        </material>
        <response_lid ident="response1" rcardinality="Single">
          <render_choice>
            <response_label ident="3637">
              <material>
                <mattext texttype="text/plain">First-person voice.</mattext>
              </material>
            </response_label>
            <response_label ident="28594">
              <material>
                <mattext texttype="text/plain">Second-person voice.</mattext>
              </material>
            </response_label>
            <response_label ident="52973">
              <material>
                <mattext texttype="text/plain">Third-person voice.</mattext>
              </material>
            </response_label>
            <response_label ident="92315">
              <material>
                <mattext texttype="text/plain">Passive voice.</mattext>
              </material>
            </response_label>
          </render_choice>
        </response_lid>
      </presentation>
      <resprocessing>
        <outcomes>
          <decvar maxvalue="100" minvalue="0" varname="SCORE" vartype="Decimal"/>
        </outcomes>
        <respcondition continue="Yes">
          <conditionvar>
            <varequal respident="response1">28594</varequal>
          </conditionvar>
          <displayfeedback feedbacktype="Response" linkrefid="28594_fb"/>
        </respcondition>
        <respcondition continue="Yes">
          <conditionvar>
            <varequal respident="response1">52973</varequal>
          </conditionvar>
          <displayfeedback feedbacktype="Response" linkrefid="52973_fb"/>
        </respcondition>
        <respcondition continue="Yes">
          <conditionvar>
            <varequal respident="response1">92315</varequal>
          </conditionvar>
          <displayfeedback feedbacktype="Response" linkrefid="92315_fb"/>
        </respcondition>
        <respcondition continue="No">
          <conditionvar>
            <varequal respident="response1">3637</varequal>
          </conditionvar>
          <setvar action="Set" varname="SCORE">100</setvar>
        </respcondition>
      </resprocessing>
      <itemfeedback ident="28594_fb">
        <flow_mat>
          <material>
            <mattext texttype="text/plain">Reflective writing primarily uses first-person voice because it centers on the writer's own experiences, thoughts, and feelings. Second-person voice uses "you" and is more common in instructional writing. Third-person voice is often used in argumentative or academic writing. Passive voice is a sentence construction style, not a point-of-view choice, and it is generally avoided in clear writing.</mattext>
          </material>
        </flow_mat>
      </itemfeedback>
      <itemfeedback ident="52973_fb">
        <flow_mat>
          <material>
            <mattext texttype="text/plain">Reflective writing primarily uses first-person voice because it centers on the writer's own experiences, thoughts, and feelings. Second-person voice uses "you" and is more common in instructional writing. Third-person voice is often used in argumentative or academic writing. Passive voice is a sentence construction style, not a point-of-view choice, and it is generally avoided in clear writing.</mattext>
          </material>
        </flow_mat>
      </itemfeedback>
      <itemfeedback ident="92315_fb">
        <flow_mat>
          <material>
            <mattext texttype="text/plain">Reflective writing primarily uses first-person voice because it centers on the writer's own experiences, thoughts, and feelings. Second-person voice uses "you" and is more common in instructional writing. Third-person voice is often used in argumentative or academic writing. Passive voice is a sentence construction style, not a point-of-view choice, and it is generally avoided in clear writing.</mattext>
          </material>
        </flow_mat>
      </itemfeedback>
    </item>
    <item ident="g5915e3342f3c3e221b806f6a20d1924e" title="Question 14">
      <itemmetadata>
        <qtimetadata>
          <qtimetadatafield>
            <fieldlabel>question_type</fieldlabel>
            <fieldentry>multiple_choice_question</fieldentry>
          </qtimetadatafield>
          <qtimetadatafield>
            <fieldlabel>points_possible</fieldlabel>
            <fieldentry>1</fieldentry>
          </qtimetadatafield>
          <qtimetadatafield>
            <fieldlabel>original_answer_ids</fieldlabel>
            <fieldentry>36558,49195,85235,48299</fieldentry>
          </qtimetadatafield>
        </qtimetadata>
      </itemmetadata>
      <presentation>
        <material>
          <mattext texttype="text/html">&lt;div&gt;What skill does the reflection stage of reflective writing require that the exploration stage does not?&lt;/div&gt;</mattext>
        </material>
        <response_lid ident="response1" rcardinality="Single">
          <render_choice>
            <response_label ident="36558">
              <material>
                <mattext texttype="text/plain">Analyzing what you learned from the experience.</mattext>
              </material>
            </response_label>
            <response_label ident="49195">
              <material>
                <mattext texttype="text/plain">Describing the basic facts of what occurred.</mattext>
              </material>
            </response_label>
            <response_label ident="85235">
              <material>
                <mattext texttype="text/plain">Listing the assignments you completed.</mattext>
              </material>
            </response_label>
            <response_label ident="48299">
              <material>
                <mattext texttype="text/plain">Recording answers to questions about the event.</mattext>
              </material>
            </response_label>
          </render_choice>
        </response_lid>
      </presentation>
      <resprocessing>
        <outcomes>
          <decvar maxvalue="100" minvalue="0" varname="SCORE" vartype="Decimal"/>
        </outcomes>
        <respcondition continue="Yes">
          <conditionvar>
            <varequal respident="response1">49195</varequal>
          </conditionvar>
          <displayfeedback feedbacktype="Response" linkrefid="49195_fb"/>
        </respcondition>
        <respcondition continue="Yes">
          <conditionvar>
            <varequal respident="response1">85235</varequal>
          </conditionvar>
          <displayfeedback feedbacktype="Response" linkrefid="85235_fb"/>
        </respcondition>
        <respcondition continue="Yes">
          <conditionvar>
            <varequal respident="response1">48299</varequal>
          </conditionvar>
          <displayfeedback feedbacktype="Response" linkrefid="48299_fb"/>
        </respcondition>
        <respcondition continue="No">
          <conditionvar>
            <varequal respident="response1">36558</varequal>
          </conditionvar>
          <setvar action="Set" varname="SCORE">100</setvar>
        </respcondition>
      </resprocessing>
      <itemfeedback ident="49195_fb">
        <flow_mat>
          <material>
            <mattext texttype="text/plain">The reflection stage moves beyond description into analysis. It asks the writer to examine the writing process, explain what was learned, and recognize changes in thinking or skills. Describing basic facts and listing assignments belong to the exploration stage. Recording answers to questions is part of exploration as well. The reflection stage requires the writer to go deeper and explain meaning.</mattext>
          </material>
        </flow_mat>
      </itemfeedback>
      <itemfeedback ident="85235_fb">
        <flow_mat>
          <material>
            <mattext texttype="text/plain">The reflection stage moves beyond description into analysis. It asks the writer to examine the writing process, explain what was learned, and recognize changes in thinking or skills. Describing basic facts and listing assignments belong to the exploration stage. Recording answers to questions is part of exploration as well. The reflection stage requires the writer to go deeper and explain meaning.</mattext>
          </material>
        </flow_mat>
      </itemfeedback>
      <itemfeedback ident="48299_fb">
        <flow_mat>
          <material>
            <mattext texttype="text/plain">The reflection stage moves beyond description into analysis. It asks the writer to examine the writing process, explain what was learned, and recognize changes in thinking or skills. Describing basic facts and listing assignments belong to the exploration stage. Recording answers to questions is part of exploration as well. The reflection stage requires the writer to go deeper and explain meaning.</mattext>
          </material>
        </flow_mat>
      </itemfeedback>
    </item>
    <item ident="g55e6f28848bd46325337ca9c907897cb" title="Question 15">
      <itemmetadata>
