        <flow_mat>
          <material>
            <mattext texttype="text/plain">The reading states that the key difference is connection: bullet points stand alone, while paragraphs connect ideas together with transition words and create a natural flow. Bullet points are not more formal than paragraphs. The reading does not state that bullet points are required for action plans. Paragraphs are associated with deeper analysis, not summary — making the final option the reverse of what the reading teaches.</mattext>
          </material>
        </flow_mat>
      </itemfeedback>
      <itemfeedback ident="23229_fb">
        <flow_mat>
          <material>
            <mattext texttype="text/plain">The reading states that the key difference is connection: bullet points stand alone, while paragraphs connect ideas together with transition words and create a natural flow. Bullet points are not more formal than paragraphs. The reading does not state that bullet points are required for action plans. Paragraphs are associated with deeper analysis, not summary — making the final option the reverse of what the reading teaches.</mattext>
          </material>
        </flow_mat>
      </itemfeedback>
