    </item>
    <item ident="ga0ddb0a4e0df7115a51b571fd27cb0ad" title="Question 4">
      <itemmetadata>
        <qtimetadata>
          <qtimetadatafield>
            <fieldlabel>question_type</fieldlabel>
            <fieldentry>multiple_choice_question</fieldentry>
          </qtimetadatafield>
          <qtimetadatafield>
            <fieldlabel>points_possible</fieldlabel>
            <fieldentry>1</fieldentry>
          </qtimetadatafield>
          <qtimetadatafield>
            <fieldlabel>original_answer_ids</fieldlabel>
            <fieldentry>3190,69777,13563,64137</fieldentry>
          </qtimetadatafield>
        </qtimetadata>
      </itemmetadata>
      <presentation>
        <material>
          <mattext texttype="text/html">&lt;div&gt;What is the main focus of the action stage in reflective writing?&lt;/div&gt;</mattext>
        </material>
        <response_lid ident="response1" rcardinality="Single">
          <render_choice>
            <response_label ident="3190">
              <material>
                <mattext texttype="text/plain">Planning how to apply insights to future situations.</mattext>
              </material>
            </response_label>
            <response_label ident="69777">
              <material>
                <mattext texttype="text/plain">Describing past events in detail.</mattext>
              </material>
            </response_label>
            <response_label ident="13563">
              <material>
                <mattext texttype="text/plain">Analyzing what you learned from an experience.</mattext>
              </material>
            </response_label>
            <response_label ident="64137">
              <material>
                <mattext texttype="text/plain">Evaluating the quality of your writing.</mattext>
              </material>
            </response_label>
          </render_choice>
        </response_lid>
      </presentation>
      <resprocessing>
        <outcomes>
          <decvar maxvalue="100" minvalue="0" varname="SCORE" vartype="Decimal"/>
        </outcomes>
        <respcondition continue="Yes">
          <conditionvar>
            <varequal respident="response1">69777</varequal>
          </conditionvar>
          <displayfeedback feedbacktype="Response" linkrefid="69777_fb"/>
        </respcondition>
        <respcondition continue="Yes">
          <conditionvar>
            <varequal respident="response1">13563</varequal>
          </conditionvar>
          <displayfeedback feedbacktype="Response" linkrefid="13563_fb"/>
        </respcondition>
        <respcondition continue="Yes">
          <conditionvar>
            <varequal respident="response1">64137</varequal>
          </conditionvar>
          <displayfeedback feedbacktype="Response" linkrefid="64137_fb"/>
        </respcondition>
        <respcondition continue="No">
          <conditionvar>
            <varequal respident="response1">3190</varequal>
          </conditionvar>
          <setvar action="Set" varname="SCORE">100</setvar>
        </respcondition>
      </resprocessing>
      <itemfeedback ident="69777_fb">
        <flow_mat>
          <material>
            <mattext texttype="text/plain">The action stage looks forward. It asks the writer to decide what to do next and plan the steps needed to reach that goal. Describing past events belongs to the exploration stage. Analyzing what you learned belongs to the reflection stage. Evaluating writing quality is an editing task, not a reflective stage.</mattext>
          </material>
        </flow_mat>
      </itemfeedback>
      <itemfeedback ident="13563_fb">
        <flow_mat>
          <material>
            <mattext texttype="text/plain">The action stage looks forward. It asks the writer to decide what to do next and plan the steps needed to reach that goal. Describing past events belongs to the exploration stage. Analyzing what you learned belongs to the reflection stage. Evaluating writing quality is an editing task, not a reflective stage.</mattext>
          </material>
        </flow_mat>
      </itemfeedback>
      <itemfeedback ident="64137_fb">
        <flow_mat>
          <material>
            <mattext texttype="text/plain">The action stage looks forward. It asks the writer to decide what to do next and plan the steps needed to reach that goal. Describing past events belongs to the exploration stage. Analyzing what you learned belongs to the reflection stage. Evaluating writing quality is an editing task, not a reflective stage.</mattext>
          </material>
        </flow_mat>
      </itemfeedback>
    </item>
    <item ident="gbbd961c1624ca047bb4edf65ca0c6543" title="Question 5">
      <itemmetadata>
        <qtimetadata>
          <qtimetadatafield>
            <fieldlabel>question_type</fieldlabel>
            <fieldentry>multiple_choice_question</fieldentry>
          </qtimetadatafield>
          <qtimetadatafield>
            <fieldlabel>points_possible</fieldlabel>
            <fieldentry>1</fieldentry>
          </qtimetadatafield>
          <qtimetadatafield>
            <fieldlabel>original_answer_ids</fieldlabel>
            <fieldentry>41412,64019,45695,6817</fieldentry>
          </qtimetadatafield>
        </qtimetadata>
      </itemmetadata>
      <presentation>
        <material>
          <mattext texttype="text/html">&lt;div&gt;How does reflective writing differ from argumentative writing in its use of evidence?&lt;/div&gt;</mattext>
        </material>
        <response_lid ident="response1" rcardinality="Single">
          <render_choice>
            <response_label ident="41412">
              <material>
                <mattext texttype="text/plain">Reflective writing draws on personal experiences, feelings, and observations as evidence.</mattext>
              </material>
            </response_label>
            <response_label ident="64019">
              <material>
                <mattext texttype="text/plain">Reflective writing draws on facts, statistics, and expert opinions as evidence.</mattext>
              </material>
            </response_label>
            <response_label ident="45695">
              <material>
                <mattext texttype="text/plain">Reflective writing does not use any evidence.</mattext>
              </material>
            </response_label>
            <response_label ident="6817">
              <material>
                <mattext texttype="text/plain">Reflective writing draws on outside research and citations as evidence.</mattext>
              </material>
            </response_label>
          </render_choice>
        </response_lid>
      </presentation>
      <resprocessing>
        <outcomes>
          <decvar maxvalue="100" minvalue="0" varname="SCORE" vartype="Decimal"/>
        </outcomes>
        <respcondition continue="Yes">
          <conditionvar>
            <varequal respident="response1">64019</varequal>
          </conditionvar>
          <displayfeedback feedbacktype="Response" linkrefid="64019_fb"/>
        </respcondition>
        <respcondition continue="Yes">
          <conditionvar>
            <varequal respident="response1">45695</varequal>
          </conditionvar>
          <displayfeedback feedbacktype="Response" linkrefid="45695_fb"/>
        </respcondition>
        <respcondition continue="Yes">
          <conditionvar>
            <varequal respident="response1">6817</varequal>
          </conditionvar>
          <displayfeedback feedbacktype="Response" linkrefid="6817_fb"/>
        </respcondition>
        <respcondition continue="No">
          <conditionvar>
            <varequal respident="response1">41412</varequal>
          </conditionvar>
          <setvar action="Set" varname="SCORE">100</setvar>
        </respcondition>
      </resprocessing>
      <itemfeedback ident="64019_fb">
        <flow_mat>
          <material>
            <mattext texttype="text/plain">Reflective writing uses the writer's own experiences, feelings, and observations to support its ideas. Facts, statistics, and expert opinions are the tools of argumentative writing. Reflective writing does include evidence — it simply comes from personal experience rather than outside sources. Citations and outside research are associated with research writing, not reflection.</mattext>
          </material>
        </flow_mat>
      </itemfeedback>
      <itemfeedback ident="45695_fb">
        <flow_mat>
          <material>
            <mattext texttype="text/plain">Reflective writing uses the writer's own experiences, feelings, and observations to support its ideas. Facts, statistics, and expert opinions are the tools of argumentative writing. Reflective writing does include evidence — it simply comes from personal experience rather than outside sources. Citations and outside research are associated with research writing, not reflection.</mattext>
          </material>
        </flow_mat>
      </itemfeedback>
      <itemfeedback ident="6817_fb">
        <flow_mat>
          <material>
            <mattext texttype="text/plain">Reflective writing uses the writer's own experiences, feelings, and observations to support its ideas. Facts, statistics, and expert opinions are the tools of argumentative writing. Reflective writing does include evidence — it simply comes from personal experience rather than outside sources. Citations and outside research are associated with research writing, not reflection.</mattext>
          </material>
        </flow_mat>
      </itemfeedback>
    </item>
    <item ident="gb3570f4f85b78f576d33be49a4042236" title="Question 6">
      <itemmetadata>
        <qtimetadata>
          <qtimetadatafield>
            <fieldlabel>question_type</fieldlabel>
            <fieldentry>multiple_choice_question</fieldentry>
          </qtimetadatafield>
          <qtimetadatafield>
            <fieldlabel>points_possible</fieldlabel>
            <fieldentry>1</fieldentry>
          </qtimetadatafield>
          <qtimetadatafield>
            <fieldlabel>original_answer_ids</fieldlabel>
            <fieldentry>2409,70754,83295,38327</fieldentry>
          </qtimetadatafield>
        </qtimetadata>
      </itemmetadata>
      <presentation>
        <material>
          <mattext texttype="text/html">&lt;div&gt;Where does the main point of a reflective essay typically appear?&lt;/div&gt;</mattext>
        </material>
        <response_lid ident="response1" rcardinality="Single">
          <render_choice>
            <response_label ident="2409">
              <material>
                <mattext texttype="text/plain">At or near the end of the essay, emerging gradually through the writing.</mattext>
              </material>
            </response_label>
            <response_label ident="70754">
              <material>
                <mattext texttype="text/plain">In the first sentence of the introduction.</mattext>
              </material>
            </response_label>
            <response_label ident="83295">
              <material>
                <mattext texttype="text/plain">In a formal thesis statement at the beginning of the essay.</mattext>
              </material>
            </response_label>
            <response_label ident="38327">
              <material>
                <mattext texttype="text/plain">In a summary paragraph at the start of the essay.</mattext>
              </material>
            </response_label>
          </render_choice>
        </response_lid>
      </presentation>
      <resprocessing>
        <outcomes>
          <decvar maxvalue="100" minvalue="0" varname="SCORE" vartype="Decimal"/>
        </outcomes>
        <respcondition continue="Yes">
          <conditionvar>
            <varequal respident="response1">70754</varequal>
          </conditionvar>
          <displayfeedback feedbacktype="Response" linkrefid="70754_fb"/>
        </respcondition>
        <respcondition continue="Yes">
          <conditionvar>
            <varequal respident="response1">83295</varequal>
          </conditionvar>
          <displayfeedback feedbacktype="Response" linkrefid="83295_fb"/>
        </respcondition>
        <respcondition continue="Yes">
          <conditionvar>
            <varequal respident="response1">38327</varequal>
          </conditionvar>
          <displayfeedback feedbacktype="Response" linkrefid="38327_fb"/>
        </respcondition>
        <respcondition continue="No">
          <conditionvar>
            <varequal respident="response1">2409</varequal>
          </conditionvar>
          <setvar action="Set" varname="SCORE">100</setvar>
        </respcondition>
      </resprocessing>
      <itemfeedback ident="70754_fb">
        <flow_mat>
          <material>
            <mattext texttype="text/plain">Reflective writing differs from argumentative writing in structure. The main point often emerges near the end, almost like a sudden realization or epiphany, as the writer works through the experience. Placing a clear thesis at the beginning is a feature of argumentative essays, not reflective ones. Reflective writers explore and discover meaning through the process of writing rather than stating conclusions upfront.</mattext>
          </material>
        </flow_mat>
      </itemfeedback>
      <itemfeedback ident="83295_fb">
        <flow_mat>
          <material>
            <mattext texttype="text/plain">Reflective writing differs from argumentative writing in structure. The main point often emerges near the end, almost like a sudden realization or epiphany, as the writer works through the experience. Placing a clear thesis at the beginning is a feature of argumentative essays, not reflective ones. Reflective writers explore and discover meaning through the process of writing rather than stating conclusions upfront.</mattext>
          </material>
        </flow_mat>
      </itemfeedback>
      <itemfeedback ident="38327_fb">
        <flow_mat>
          <material>
            <mattext texttype="text/plain">Reflective writing differs from argumentative writing in structure. The main point often emerges near the end, almost like a sudden realization or epiphany, as the writer works through the experience. Placing a clear thesis at the beginning is a feature of argumentative essays, not reflective ones. Reflective writers explore and discover meaning through the process of writing rather than stating conclusions upfront.</mattext>
          </material>
        </flow_mat>
      </itemfeedback>
    </item>
    <item ident="g2f62a78395a0677c168860a7971e9deb" title="Question 7">
      <itemmetadata>
        <qtimetadata>
          <qtimetadatafield>
            <fieldlabel>question_type</fieldlabel>
            <fieldentry>multiple_choice_question</fieldentry>
          </qtimetadatafield>
          <qtimetadatafield>
            <fieldlabel>points_possible</fieldlabel>
            <fieldentry>1</fieldentry>
          </qtimetadatafield>
          <qtimetadatafield>
            <fieldlabel>original_answer_ids</fieldlabel>
            <fieldentry>90858,3376,45905,76051</fieldentry>
          </qtimetadatafield>
        </qtimetadata>
      </itemmetadata>
      <presentation>
        <material>
          <mattext texttype="text/html">&lt;div&gt;What does the acronym SMART stand for in the context of goal setting for writing improvement?&lt;/div&gt;</mattext>
        </material>
        <response_lid ident="response1" rcardinality="Single">
          <render_choice>
            <response_label ident="90858">
              <material>
                <mattext texttype="text/plain">Specific, Measurable, Achievable, Relevant, Time-bound.</mattext>
              </material>
            </response_label>
            <response_label ident="3376">
              <material>
                <mattext texttype="text/plain">Simple, Meaningful, Accurate, Realistic, Timely.</mattext>
              </material>
            </response_label>
            <response_label ident="45905">
              <material>
                <mattext texttype="text/plain">Strategic, Manageable, Appropriate, Reasonable, Tested.</mattext>
              </material>
            </response_label>
            <response_label ident="76051">
              <material>
                <mattext texttype="text/plain">Structured, Motivated, Attainable, Resourced, Tracked.</mattext>
              </material>
            </response_label>
          </render_choice>
        </response_lid>
      </presentation>
      <resprocessing>
        <outcomes>
          <decvar maxvalue="100" minvalue="0" varname="SCORE" vartype="Decimal"/>
        </outcomes>
        <respcondition continue="Yes">
          <conditionvar>
            <varequal respident="response1">3376</varequal>
          </conditionvar>
          <displayfeedback feedbacktype="Response" linkrefid="3376_fb"/>
        </respcondition>
        <respcondition continue="Yes">
          <conditionvar>
            <varequal respident="response1">45905</varequal>
          </conditionvar>
          <displayfeedback feedbacktype="Response" linkrefid="45905_fb"/>
        </respcondition>
        <respcondition continue="Yes">
          <conditionvar>
            <varequal respident="response1">76051</varequal>
          </conditionvar>
          <displayfeedback feedbacktype="Response" linkrefid="76051_fb"/>
        </respcondition>
        <respcondition continue="No">
          <conditionvar>
            <varequal respident="response1">90858</varequal>
          </conditionvar>
          <setvar action="Set" varname="SCORE">100</setvar>
        </respcondition>
      </resprocessing>
      <itemfeedback ident="3376_fb">
        <flow_mat>
          <material>
            <mattext texttype="text/plain">The SMART framework used in the course reading stands for Specific, Measurable, Achievable, Relevant, and Time-bound. Each element helps a writer create a goal that leads to real progress rather than remaining vague or unachievable. The other options use similar-sounding words but do not match the framework defined in the reading.</mattext>
          </material>
        </flow_mat>
      </itemfeedback>
      <itemfeedback ident="45905_fb">
